.SH FILES
.I "Table B-1. What conn reads and writes"
.RS
.TP
\fB~/.config/conn/config.json\fR
the configuration; Section 9
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/tmux\-<uid>.sock\fR
the socket of the tmux server that holds the shells
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/tmux.conf\fR
the tmux configuration conn writes at every launch; your own .tmux.conf is not
read
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/latest\-release\fR
the latest release as last checked, and when
.TP
\fB.conn\fR
a project's plan; Section 6
.RE
.TP
B-1.
The shells are held by a tmux server of conn's own, one per user, on the socket
above. It is never something you have to reach; \fBtmux \-S
~/.local/state/conn/tmux\-<uid>.sock attach\fR is what \fBconn\fR does when it
opens the window.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.I "Table C-1. Variables conn reads"
.RS
.TP
\fBCONN_SOCKET\fR
where the tmux server listens, instead of the state directory
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
where the configuration lives, instead of ~/.config
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
where the socket and the tmux configuration live, instead of ~/.local/state
.TP
\fBSHELL\fR
the shell \fBs\fR opens, and the one behind \fBa\fR, \fBA\fR, \fBr\fR and the
tasks
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
set, the navigator draws without color, as no-color.org asks; CLICOLOR_FORCE and
TERM=dumb are honored too
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
where Claude Code's session files are read from, instead of ~/.claude
.TP
\fBOLLAMA_MODELS\fR
where ollama's models are read from, instead of ~/.ollama/models
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.I "Table D-1. How conn ends"
.RS
.TP
\fB0\fR
a clean exit
.TP
\fB1\fR
conn or its server failed
.TP
\fB2\fR
an argument conn does not understand
.RE
